      "hints": [
        {
          "if": "Freight rates jump quickly",
          "then": "Usually demand meeting an almost fully used fleet: a few percent more demand can lift rates a lot. Try it in Analytics → Freight rate lab."
        },
        {
          "if": "Ships reroute or a chokepoint is attacked",
          "then": "Longer routes mean more ton-miles, which absorbs ships and lifts rates. War-risk premiums for the area rise too."
        },
        {
          "if": "Many newbuilding orders are reported",
          "then": "More ships arrive in two to four years. Good news for shipyards today, a warning sign for future freight rates."
        },
        {
          "if": "You see a broker's weekly report",
          "then": "The best free view of what was actually fixed this week and at which rates. Read the dry bulk, tanker and S&P sections side by side."
